# Entry point of the self-hosted toolchain. The hidden golden-dump modes below
# exist for the differential: their output must stay byte-identical against the
# previous release (scripts/selfhost-prev-diff.sh), which is the oracle now that
# the Kotlin implementation is archived at kotlin-final. An intentional change
# is declared with an `Emit-Change(<label>):` line in the commit message, one
# label per line, each registered in scripts/emit-labels.txt -- the bare form
# and a wildcard are both hard errors, since either blinds the whole oracle.
#   selfhost lex <file>...                the token stream (dawn __lex)
#   selfhost parse <file>...              the parsed AST   (dawn __parse)
#   selfhost check [--std <dir>] <t>...   diagnostics + pub surface + const
#                                         values (dawn __check); a target is a
#                                         file (use-closure) or a project dir
#   selfhost emit <t> -o <dir>            every class of the program (dawn __emit)
#   selfhost build <t> -o <out.jar>       executable jar; --vendor <pkg> packs
#                                         class-path packages in (standalone)

